      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 42. —कंदर्प—Káma, the god of love; cf. कंदर्पयामीति मदा-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ज्जातमात्रो जगाद च । तेन कंदर्पनामानं तं चकार चतुर्भुजः ॥ किं कदर्थ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "यसि—why do you trouble your hand. टङ्कारितैः—टङ्कारवैः v. l.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "टङ्क+आरव; टङ्कायतीति ( fr. टङ्क+अच् ) or टामिति शब्दं कायतीति",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "टङ्कः an onomatopœic word. टङ्कारित however is better and has",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "therefore been preferred. For the third line cf. supra. बाले लीला-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "मुकुलितममी &c. Mis. sl. 40. स्निग्ध affectionate; विदग्ध cleverly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "cast, artful.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 43. उन्मीलत् &c.—त्रिवली the folds of skin above the navel",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of a woman regarded as a mark of beauty ( Cf. Kum. I. 39 ),",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "डयत् &c. pairs of Chakravàka birds are usually described as",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "haunting river-banks. क्रूराशया has two meanings (1) क्रूराः आशयाः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "यस्याम् in which there are dangerous aquatic animals; (2) क्रूरा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "आशयाः thoughts (or आशय mind) यस्याः। संसारार्णव–Samsára is the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "sea to which the river, in the form of a woman, leads a man.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 44. हतपरमार्थैः—The Indriyas which are often compared",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "to horses, tempt a man further and further away from real",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "bliss ( मोक्ष ).",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
